<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ sees NZ$25 mln costs in 96/97.</title>
<headline>Air NZ sees NZ$25 mln costs in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air New Zealand Ltd said on Wednesday it expects to make NZ$100 million in cost savings in the 1997/98 year, but would incur one-off costs of $25 million in this financial year, in part arising from staff reductions.</p>
<p>In reporting a half year profit of NZ$76.74 million, down from $135.1 million, the carrier also said the benefits of its half share in Ansett Australia would not be fully reflected in its finanical results until the 1997/98 financial year.</p>
<p>This would also be the case in respect to the benefits which would flow from the alliance arrangements with United Airlines when that alliance comes into effect in April this year.  </p>
<p>Air NZ earlier reported a 43.2 percent decline in first half earnings to NZ$76.7 million, exactly in line with market expectations.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
